[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mollama_kimi-k2.6_cloud-failing-tests-trial-3[0m[0m
All 15 tests pass. Here's what I fixed in `src/`:

**`src/auth.py`**
- `has_permission` was doing a literal `in` check instead of case-insensitive comparison. Changed to lowercase both the required role and each user role before comparing.
- `is_admin_or_owner` used `and` instead of `or`, requiring the user to be both admin AND owner. Changed to `or` so either condition grants access.

**`src/inventory.py`**
- `__init__` used a mutable default dict `{}`, causing all `Inventory()` instances to share state. Changed to `None` with `dict(initial) if initial is not None else {}`.
- `add` replaced the stock count (`self._stock[sku] = qty`) instead of accumulating. Changed to `self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`.
- `reserve` used `>=` so reserving the exact available amount raised `OutOfStock`. Changed to `>` to allow reserving up to the full available quantity.
- `release` allowed reserved quantity to go negative. Added a guard that raises `ValueError` if `current - qty < 0`.

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- `slugify` preserved uppercase characters. Changed to append `char.lower()` for alphanumeric characters.
- `slugify`'s `replace("--", "-")` only collapsed one layer of doubled separators. Changed to a `while "--" in collapsed` loop to fully collapse any run of repeated dashes.
- `truncate` appended the suffix on top of `max_len`, producing output longer than the limit. Changed to `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix` so the total length never exceeds `max_len`.
